					<div class="xsmall">3/19/2002 - 6:46 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2645">Cuedyen Abuhannah</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2878">Legween Abuhannah</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														My turn,<br />
<br />
First, everyone is entitled to an opinion.  In the military, I used to tell the guys below me if I wanted there opinion I would give it to them.  Guilds with that type of attitude have problems and I encourage everyone to be open.<br />
<br />
I join a guilds for the family style atmosphere.  DF did it for me originally, think I joined the guild shortly after it was formed.  I left because of what I perceived as mistreatment of Salorn and the abuse of the charter.<br />
<br />
While my main is a lvl 51 paly, it took me 40+ game days to get there.  The only guildie I know that has taken longer is Aamain.  I suspect that Salorn/Minvardar spent a good amount of time leveling.  For me, getting people to lvl 50 is neither here nor there.  Play the game for fun period - for me grinding is not fun.<br />
<br />
I also have extreme heartburn with Power Leveling and will not participate in it.  However, I also do not judge you if you decide that power leveling is your thing.  I will help lowbies and teach skills if asked - but I will not stay around to make leveling easier.  <br />
<br />
You will see my druid in newbie zones buffing and healing anyone I see - true newbies love it.  I had a kickass time in GFay last week trying to turn all the newbies into wolves :)  Also, during my time there I found two friends on alts and both joined the guild - one twinked the other playing the low game the way it was meant to be played.  I judged neither of them because they were both having fun - and that is the point of this game.<br />
<br />
I am a loner type in RL and sometimes I drift into that mode while playing.  I also play for a few minutes here and there - makes it hard to group with guildies.  But, I will make a concentrated effort to group with guildies more.  <br />
<br />
Finally, guild officers provide leadership but the backbone has to be the regular members.  Everyone needs to contribute or we become just another guild.  <br />
<br />
Family and fun :)						</td>
